---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research — Sachleen Singh"
  description="Dissertation research on ONT methylation, gene regulatory networks, and single-nucleus multiome analysis in soybean."
>
  <h1>Research</h1>
  <p class="intro">
    My dissertation investigates how soybean plants mount a defense response against pathogens,
    using three complementary computational approaches.
  </p>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>ONT Methylation Profiling</h2>
    <p>
      Long-read DNA sequencing with Oxford Nanopore Technology lets us measure chemical
      modifications on DNA (methylation) that affect which genes are turned on or off. This
      chapter profiles genome-wide cytosine methylation patterns in soybean plants responding
      to pathogen infection, identifying regulatory regions that may coordinate the defense
      response without requiring bisulfite conversion.
    </p>
    <p class="technical-note">
      Methods: Oxford Nanopore sequencing, Modkit, bismark-free methylation calling, differential
      methylation analysis.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>Gene Regulatory Network Inference</h2>
    <p>
      Gene regulatory networks describe which transcription factors control which target genes.
      This chapter applies computational inference methods to RNA-sequencing data from infected
      soybean tissue to reconstruct the regulatory wiring underlying disease resistance, revealing
      candidate master regulators of the immune response.
    </p>
    <p class="technical-note">
      Methods: RNA-seq, GENIE3, ARACNE, network topology analysis, transcription factor enrichment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>SCENIC+ Single-Nucleus Analysis</h2>
    <p>
      Single-nucleus multiome sequencing measures gene expression and chromatin accessibility
      simultaneously in individual cells. This chapter applies the SCENIC+ framework to soybean
      defense data to map gene regulatory programs at single-cell resolution, linking transcription
      factor activity to cell-type-specific responses during infection.
    </p>
    <p class="technical-note">
      Methods: snRNA-seq, snATAC-seq, SCENIC+, eRegulon inference, cell-type annotation.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
    margin-bottom: 2.5em;
    font-size: 1.05em;
  }

  .chapter {
    margin-bottom: 3em;
    padding-bottom: 3em;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
  }

  .chapter:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .chapter h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75em;
    font-size: 1.5em;
  }

  .technical-note {
    font-size: 0.875em;
    color: rgb(var(--gray));
    margin-top: 0.5em;
  }
</style>
